   "value": "**[3,1,0] run** (same code, first cell switched to `Λ = {3, 1, 0}`):\n\n| check | result |\n|---|---|\n| (a) Omega_c[om] exact left eigencovector of one-site S2, S3 (u0, u1, u2, all Laurent coefficients, Laurent fit exact), twist gc[om], both theta, at 4 om | {{True, True}, {True, True}, {True, True}, {True, True}} |\n| (a) control: Omega_D[zeta, om] (not companion) is NOT an eigencovector of the companion-twist one-site operators (expected False) | {False, False} |\n| (b) Gauss parameters (alpha, beta, gamma) = (U12, U13 - U12 U23, U23) of the unipotent of Omega_c[om] (symbolic, Factor) | {o1^(-1), -(1/(o1*o2)), (o1 + o2)/(o1*o2)} |\n| (b) numeric check: coverG[gaussC at wP] == OmegaC[wP] exactly | True |\n| (b) om2 -> infinity limit of (alpha, beta, gamma) (om1, om3 fixed) | {o1^(-1), 0, o1^(-1)} |\n| (b) limit has beta = 0 and alpha = gamma (XXX gaussCov{a,0,a} pattern)? | {True, True} |\n| (b) limit independent of om3? | True |\n| PphysG[zeta] (rep image) = rho((PauxG^-1)^T): matrix Pphys3 == Transpose[Inverse[PauxG]] exactly at P, P', and a third point | {True, True, True} |\n| (c) frame tie: OmegaD[zeta, om].PphysG[zeta] parallel to Omega_c[om] exactly, 4 points | {True, True, True, True} |\n| (c) kappa^G measured = first component of OmegaD.PphysG (Omega_c[[1]] = 1): values at 4 points | {-75600/1331, 6561/343, -629856/265837, 625/343} |\n| (c) XXX kappaTie formula Prod_k Det[(n.P3)_{1..k,1..k}]^(lambda_k - lambda_{k+1}) equals kappa^G for each P3 variant (4 points) | {\"P3 = PauxG^-T\" -> {True, True, True, True}, \"P3 = PauxG^T (inverse of PauxG^-T)\" -> {False, False, False, False}, \"P3 = PauxG^-1\" -> {False, False, False, False}, \"P3 = PauxG\" -> {False, False, False, False}} |\n| (c) closed form of the minors: Delta_k(n.PauxG^-T), k = 1, 2, 3 (symbolic, Factor); kappa^G = Delta1^(l1-l2) Delta2^(l2-l3) Delta3^(l3) | {o1^2/((f2 - o1)*(f3 - o1)), -((o1*o2)/((f1 - f2)*(f3 - o1)*(f3 - o2))), 1/((f1 - f2)*(f1 - f3)*(-f2 + f3))} |\n| (c) om2 -> infinity limits of the minors Delta_k (finite? Factor) | {-(o1^2/((f2 - o1)*(-f3 + o1))), -(o1/((f1 - f2)*(-f3 + o1))), -(1/((f1 - f2)*(f1 - f3)*(f2 - f3)))} |\n| (c) kappa^G at om2 = 10^6, 10^9, 10^12 (P, om1 = 5/2) and its predicted limit (Prod Delta_k,inf^(l_k - l_k+1)) | {{-40.5710262960360631224643205609870606931`12., -40.57099927573253194891059355071374906887`12., -40.57099924871224643125471374906085651089`12.}, -40.57099924868519909842223891810668670173`12.} |\n| (c) tie of the limits: OmegaDinf[zeta, om1].PphysG[zeta] parallel to coverG[gaussCinf(om1, om3)] exactly (P, P'; om1 = 5/2, -2/5; om3 = 3/5, 9/4) | {{{True, True}, {True, True}}, {{True, True}, {True, True}}} |\n| (c) kappa^G_inf(zeta, om1) = first component of OmegaDinf.PphysG at P (om1 = 5/2, -2/5, 9/7) | {-54000/1331, -3/242, -102036672/2197} |",
