   "value": "### Task A result (both reps): the Gaudin (inf,inf) family IS CG-complete\n\n**A1.** r_1^inf = (w1-z1)/(w1-z2), r_2^inf = -(w1-z1)(z2-z3)/((z1-z2)(w1-z3)), r_3^inf = (w1-z2)(z1-z3)/((z1-z2)(w1-z3)) are exactly the om2 -> infinity limits of the round-1 r_k (symbolic `Limit`), equal to the `Infinity` branch of `rGauss`, and `OmegaD[zeta,{om1,10^k}]` converges to `OmegaDinf` with relative error 6.4e-7, 6.4e-10, 6.4e-13 for k = 6, 9, 12. `OmegaD` depends on (om1, om2) only (om3 never appears; the eigencovector property of the two-site vacuum holds for any om3). The Laurent-coefficient operators H1, H2, S3c[s,1], S3c[s,2] at twist g'(om1, om2, om3) are exact polynomials of degree 1 in om2 (not 2 for S3: the rank-one limit of g'/om2 kills the quadratic terms); OmegaDinf (x) OmegaDinf is an exact left eigencovector of the top-degree coefficient of each, with eigenvalues (om3 = 3/5) H_s: 2 ([2,1,0]) / 3 ([3,1,0]) = lambda_1, S3c[s,1]: lambda_1 om3, S3c[s,2]: 0, and it is the UNIQUE common eigencovector (null space dimension 1). So the family is the eigencovector family of the rescaled limit operators (a finite limit exists).\n\n**A2.** Omega_c[om] = e1 rho(U of PauxG[om]^-T) is the exact left eigencovector of the one-site S2, S3 (all u, all Laurent coefficients, both theta, four om). Its Gauss parameters are (alpha, beta, gamma) = (1/om1, -1/(om1 om2), (om1+om2)/(om1 om2)); om2 -> infinity gives (1/om1, 0, 1/om1): beta = 0 and alpha = gamma = 1/om1, independent of om3 (the XXX gaussCov{a,0,a} pattern). Frame tie: OmegaD[zeta,om].PphysG[zeta] is parallel to Omega_c[om] exactly (4 points), with PphysG = rho((PauxG^-1)^T) (the matrix Pphys3 equals (PauxG^-1)^T exactly), and kappa^G(zeta,om) = first component of OmegaD.PphysG = Delta1^(l1-l2) Delta2^(l2-l3) Delta3^(l3), Delta1 = om1^2/((z2-om1)(z3-om1)), Delta2 = -om1 om2/((z1-z2)(z3-om1)(z3-om2)), Delta3 = 1/((z1-z2)(z1-z3)(z3-z2)): this IS the XXX kappaTie formula Prod_k Det[(n.P3)_{1..k,1..k}]^(l_k-l_{k+1}) with n = nMat3[zeta,om] and **P3 = (PauxG^-1)^T** (the other three variants P3 = PauxG^T, PauxG^-1, PauxG all fail). As om2 -> infinity kappa^G stays finite (Delta1 -> om1^2/((om1-z2)(om1-z3)), Delta2 -> -om1/((z1-z2)(om1-z3)), Delta3 unchanged) and OmegaDinf.PphysG is parallel to coverG[(1/om1, 0, 1/om1)] exactly.\n\n**A3.** Exact undo of Phi^inf at 11 points (P, P', one generic, eight regime points). The undone Gauss parameters are eps-free (asserted symbolically): a' = (z1-z2)(om1-om1')/((z2-om1)(z2-om1')), c' = (z1-z3)(z2-z3)(om1-om1')/((z1-z2)(z3-om1)(z3-om1')), g' = (z3-z1)(z3-z2)(om1-om1')/((z3-om1)(z2-om1')(z3-om1')) (the XXX leading coefficients at om2 = om2' = infinity). Jacobian rank of (oh1, oh1') -> (a', c', g') = 2 at four points. **Per-weight ranks of phi_u over the 4-point grid equal the weight multiplicities on EVERY weight of V (adjoint: the weight (1,1,1) of multiplicity 2 gets rank 2; [3,1,0]: the three weights of multiplicity 2 get rank 2), also over 6 points and for the second direction phi'. The family is CG-complete in Gaudin; no fallback is needed.**\n\n**A4.** K/S = O(eps) for every HW branch of both reps (max|K/S| doubles with eps, ratios 2.000; K = 0 for the top branch), S = O(1) (eps-exponent 0), undo S = <phi_u (x) e1|P_HW Psi> to 1e-190. CG at leading order from the overlap alone reproduces the exact G-norm-1 HW-ket slices (1-dim slices and the 2-dim slices from pairs of grid points: (3,2,1) for [2,1,0]; (5,2,1), (4,3,1), (4,2,2) for [3,1,0]) with relative error 1e-18 .. 1e-21 after Richardson (raw error exactly O(eps), ratio 4.00 between 4e-6 and 1e-6). Octet mixing: R_c = 5.854101966250, -0.854101966250 (roots of R^2 - 5R - 5 = 0; overlap-extracted agree to 9.4e-18 and 1.9e-19 relative); [3,1,0] (5,2,1): 4.311737691490, -0.811737691490. **Controls:** (i) om1' = om1 gives Phi = Omega (x) Omega, a' = c' = g' = 0, and only the top branch is read (all other branches \"not read\"); (ii) om1' = 7/4 fixed (not scaled) with om2 = om2' = infinity **fails**, unlike round 1 at finite om2: the limit eps -> 0 of phi_u has rank 1 on every multiplicity-2 weight, the singlet-type branches (adjoint (2,2,2): K/S = 0.517; [3,1,0] (4,2,2): 0.465, (3,3,2): 0.388) have K/S = O(1) and all 2-dim slices are wrong by O(1) (e.g. adjoint (3,2,1) copy 1: 0.96 relative).\n\n**A5.** Reference tables: markdown tables in the A5 results (cells following the A5 code cell; [2,1,0] and [3,1,0] blocks): A5-1 at P (all states), A5-2 at P' (all states), A5-3 regime point eps = 1e-6 (HW branches).\n",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## Task B: the [3,1,0] fourth localiser (Lambda = {3,1,0} only; exact at P and P')\n### B1/B2: the localising subspace L inside D2 (rank 26), and sparse representatives of the extra direction\n",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "If[Λ === {3, 1, 0},\n(* Task B1/B2. Generators: D1 = {id, W, H1, S3c[1,2], S3c[1,1], S3c[2,2], S3c[2,1]} (7, independent) and the 21 quadratic monomials Q_ij = a_i a_j (i <= j) of the six non-identity elements a = {W, H1, S3c12, S3c11, S3c22, S3c21} (all commute): 28 generators spanning D2 (rank 26 expected). The operator X = Sum c_g g localises at site 1 iff Phi_X . k = 0 for all k in K = NullSpace[{Omega1}], Phi_X = reshape(<Omega (x) Omega|X, 15 x 15) (rows = site 1); at site 2 iff k . Phi_X = 0. <Omega (x) Omega|g is computed by pushing the covector through the factors (no 225 x 225 products). Operators are compared through an exact sketch (action on three random integer vectors) that is faithful on the 28-dim generator space (rank checked). L := {X in D2 : localises}; dim L (as an operator space), dim L cap D1, quotient, and l = dim of the image covector space. *)\nck = <||>;\n(* two generator bases (same span D1, D2): basis 1 = site-1 variables {W, H1, S3c12, S3c11, S3c22, S3c21}; basis 2 = site-2 variables {W, H2t = H1 + W (= -H2 + const), S3c22, S3c21, S3c12, S3c11} *)\nbBaseNames = <|1 -> {\"W\", \"H1\", \"S3c12\", \"S3c11\", \"S3c22\", \"S3c21\"}, 2 -> {\"W\", \"H2t\", \"S3c22\", \"S3c21\", \"S3c12\", \"S3c11\"}|>;\nbNames[b_] := Join[{\"id\"}, bBaseNames[b], Flatten[Table[bBaseNames[b][[i]] <> \".\" <> bBaseNames[b][[j]], {i, 6}, {j, i, 6}]]];\nbPairs = Flatten[Table[{i, j}, {i, 6}, {j, i, 6}], 1];\nSeedRandom[20261016];\nbW = Table[RandomInteger[{-9, 9}, d2], {3}];\nbSetup[zz_, ww_, ths_, basis_] := bSetup[zz, ww, ths, basis] = Module[{L = laurent[DiagonalMatrix[zz], ths], Wo, a, Om1, O2, K, actRow, actCol, rows, Phis, Sk},\n  Wo = SparseArray[Sum[zz[[k]] (E1[k, k] + E2[k, k]), {k, 3}]];\n  a = If[basis == 1, {Wo, L[\"Hres\"][[1]], L[\"S3c\"][{1, 2}], L[\"S3c\"][{1, 1}], L[\"S3c\"][{2, 2}], L[\"S3c\"][{2, 1}]}, {Wo, L[\"Hres\"][[1]] + Wo, L[\"S3c\"][{2, 2}], L[\"S3c\"][{2, 1}], L[\"S3c\"][{1, 2}], L[\"S3c\"][{1, 1}]}];\n  Om1 = ΩD[zz, ww[[1 ;; 2]]]; O2 = kron[Om1, Om1]; K = NullSpace[{Om1}];\n  actRow[r_, g_] := If[g == 1, r, If[g <= 7, r . a[[g - 1]], (r . a[[bPairs[[g - 7, 1]]]]) . a[[bPairs[[g - 7, 2]]]]]];\n  actCol[w_, g_] := If[g == 1, w, If[g <= 7, a[[g - 1]] . w, a[[bPairs[[g - 7, 1]]]] . (a[[bPairs[[g - 7, 2]]]] . w)]];\n  Phis = Table[Partition[actRow[O2, g], d1], {g, 28}];\n  Sk = Table[Flatten[Table[actCol[w, g], {w, bW}]], {g, 28}];\n  <|\"zz\" -> zz, \"ww\" -> ww, \"ths\" -> ths, \"basis\" -> basis, \"names\" -> bNames[basis], \"a\" -> a, \"Om1\" -> Om1, \"K\" -> K, \"Phis\" -> Phis, \"Sk\" -> Sk, \"actRow\" -> actRow, \"actCol\" -> actCol|>];\nbLocCols[sc_, site_] := Table[Flatten[If[site == 1, sc[\"Phis\"][[g]] . Transpose[sc[\"K\"]], sc[\"K\"] . sc[\"Phis\"][[g]]]], {g, 28}];\nbVec[sc_, site_] := If[site == 1, Table[sc[\"Phis\"][[g, All, 1]], {g, 28}], Table[sc[\"Phis\"][[g, 1, All]], {g, 28}]];\nbAnalyse[sc_, site_] := Module[{A = Transpose[bLocCols[sc, site]], ns, nsD1, rkSk, dimL, dimLD1, vs, ell, vsD1, ell3},\n  rkSk = MatrixRank[sc[\"Sk\"]]; ns = NullSpace[A]; nsD1 = NullSpace[A[[All, 1 ;; 7]]];\n  dimL = MatrixRank[ns . sc[\"Sk\"]]; dimLD1 = Length[nsD1];\n  vs = If[ns === {}, {}, ns . bVec[sc, site]]; ell = If[vs === {}, 0, MatrixRank[vs]];\n  <|\"rkSk\" -> rkSk, \"rkD1\" -> MatrixRank[sc[\"Sk\"][[1 ;; 7]]], \"nullGen\" -> Length[ns], \"dimL\" -> dimL, \"dimLD1\" -> dimLD1, \"quot\" -> dimL - dimLD1, \"ell\" -> ell, \"ns\" -> ns, \"nsD1\" -> nsD1|>];\n{tB1, bP} = AbsoluteTiming[bSetup[zP, wP, thN, 1]];\nbQ = bSetup[zQ, wQ, thN, 1]; bP2 = bSetup[zP, wP, thN, 2]; bQ2 = bSetup[zQ, wQ, thN, 2];\nbAnP = {bAnalyse[bP, 1], bAnalyse[bP2, 2]}; bAnQ = {bAnalyse[bQ, 1], bAnalyse[bQ2, 2]};\nck[\"rank of the 28 generators (sketch) = rank D2, rank of D1 (P, P')\"] = {bAnP[[1]][\"rkSk\"], bAnP[[1]][\"rkD1\"], bAnQ[[1]][\"rkSk\"], bAnQ[[1]][\"rkD1\"]};\nck[\"site 1, P: {dim L (operators), dim L cap D1, quotient, l = dim of the covector space v(L)}\"] = Table[bAnP[[1]][k], {k, {\"dimL\", \"dimLD1\", \"quot\", \"ell\"}}];\nck[\"site 1, P': same\"] = Table[bAnQ[[1]][k], {k, {\"dimL\", \"dimLD1\", \"quot\", \"ell\"}}];\nck[\"site 2, P: same\"] = Table[bAnP[[2]][k], {k, {\"dimL\", \"dimLD1\", \"quot\", \"ell\"}}];\nck[\"site 2, P': same\"] = Table[bAnQ[[2]][k], {k, {\"dimL\", \"dimLD1\", \"quot\", \"ell\"}}];\n(* which D1 elements localise on their own, and the coefficient vectors of L cap D1 (row-reduced, on {id, W, H1, S3c12, S3c11, S3c22, S3c21}) *)\nck[\"site 1, P: L cap D1 coefficient vectors (RowReduce) on the basis-1 D1 = {id, W, H1, S3c12, S3c11, S3c22, S3c21}\"] = RowReduce[bAnP[[1]][\"nsD1\"]];\nck[\"site 2, P: L cap D1 coefficient vectors (RowReduce) on the basis-2 D1 = {id, W, H2t, S3c22, S3c21, S3c12, S3c11}\"] = RowReduce[bAnP[[2]][\"nsD1\"]];\n(* B2: supports of size 1, 2, 3 among the 21 quadratic monomials, with free D1 coefficients *)\nbSupportScan[sc_, site_, maxs_] := Module[{A = Transpose[bLocCols[sc, site]], Sk = sc[\"Sk\"], sk1 = sc[\"Sk\"][[1 ;; 7]], rk1, res = {}},\n  rk1 = MatrixRank[sc[\"Sk\"][[1 ;; 7]]];\n  Do[Do[Module[{cols = Join[Range[7], 7 + S], ns, outside, reach},\n    ns = NullSpace[A[[All, cols]]];\n    If[ns =!= {},\n     reach = And @@ Table[AnyTrue[ns, #[[7 + m]] =!= 0 &], {m, Length[S]}];\n     outside = AnyTrue[ns, MatrixRank[Append[sk1, #[[1 ;; 7]] . sk1 + #[[8 ;;]] . Sk[[7 + S]]]] > rk1 &];\n     If[reach && outside, AppendTo[res, <|\"S\" -> S, \"ns\" -> ns|>]]]], {S, Subsets[Range[21], {sz}]}], {sz, maxs}];\n  res];\nminimalSupports[res_] := Select[res, Function[r, ! AnyTrue[res, #[\"S\"] =!= r[\"S\"] && SubsetQ[r[\"S\"], #[\"S\"]] &]]];\n(* explicit X for a support: reduced row echelon with the quadratic columns first, so that the D1 coefficients on the pivot columns of L cap D1 vanish *)\nbExplicit[r_, nm_] := Module[{S = r[\"S\"], ns = r[\"ns\"], M, rr, rows},\n  M = ns[[All, Join[7 + Range[Length[S]], Range[7]]]]; rr = RowReduce[M];\n  rows = Select[rr, ! (# [[1 ;; Length[S]]] === ConstantArray[0, Length[S]]) &];\n  Table[StringRiffle[Join[Table[If[row[[k]] === 0, Nothing, ToString[row[[k]], InputForm] <> \"*\" <> nm[[7 + S[[k]]]]], {k, Length[S]}], Table[If[row[[Length[S] + j]] === 0, Nothing, ToString[row[[Length[S] + j]], InputForm] <> \"*\" <> nm[[j]]], {j, 7}]], \" + \"], {row, rows}]];\nbScans = <||>;\nbPts = <|{\"P\", 1} -> bP, {\"P\", 2} -> bP2, {\"P'\", 1} -> bQ, {\"P'\", 2} -> bQ2|>;\n{tScans, dummy} = AbsoluteTiming[Do[bScans[k] = bSupportScan[bPts[k], k[[2]], 3], {k, Keys[bPts]}]];\nck[\"B2 time of the four scans (supports of size <= 3 among the 21 quadratics, 1561 systems each, free D1 coefficients), s\"] = tScans;\nDo[ck[\"B2 \" <> k[[1]] <> \", site \" <> ToString[k[[2]]] <> \" (basis \" <> ToString[k[[2]]] <> \"): # supports found by size {1,2,3}; minimal supports\"] = {Table[Count[Length[#[\"S\"]] & /@ bScans[k], sz], {sz, 3}], bNames[k[[2]]][[7 + #[\"S\"]]] & /@ minimalSupports[bScans[k]]}, {k, Keys[bScans]}];\nDo[ck[\"B2 \" <> k[[1]] <> \", site \" <> ToString[k[[2]]] <> \": explicit X for each minimal support (q-part first, D1 part reduced modulo L cap D1)\"] = Table[{bNames[k[[2]]][[7 + r[\"S\"]]], bExplicit[r, bNames[k[[2]]]]}, {r, minimalSupports[bScans[k]]}], {k, Keys[bScans]}];\nbNat1 = {\"H1.H1\", \"H1.S3c12\", \"S3c12.S3c12\", \"H1.S3c11\", \"S3c12.S3c11\", \"S3c11.S3c11\", \"W.H1\", \"W.S3c12\"};\nbNat2 = {\"H2t.H2t\", \"H2t.S3c22\", \"S3c22.S3c22\", \"H2t.S3c21\", \"S3c22.S3c21\", \"S3c21.S3c21\", \"W.H2t\", \"W.S3c22\"};\nck[\"B2 natural candidates, site 1 (P): {name, single-monomial support works, appears in a support found}\"] = Table[With[{pos = Position[bNames[1], nm][[1, 1]] - 7}, {nm, MemberQ[bScans[{\"P\", 1}][[All, \"S\"]], {pos}], AnyTrue[bScans[{\"P\", 1}][[All, \"S\"]], MemberQ[#, pos] &]}], {nm, bNat1}];\nck[\"B2 natural candidates, site 2 (P, basis 2): same\"] = Table[With[{pos = Position[bNames[2], nm][[1, 1]] - 7}, {nm, MemberQ[bScans[{\"P\", 2}][[All, \"S\"]], {pos}], AnyTrue[bScans[{\"P\", 2}][[All, \"S\"]], MemberQ[#, pos] &]}], {nm, bNat2}];\nck[\"B1 note: the individual D1 elements S3c11, S3c22, S3c21, W do not localise on their own at site 1 (L cap D1 has dim 3: id, H1, S3c12; site 2: id, W + H1, S3c22)\"] = True;\nchecks = Join[checks, ck];\nGrid[Join[{{\"check\", \"result\"}}, List @@@ Normal[ck]], Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]\n, Grid[{{\"Task B is [3,1,0]-only: skipped for this Λ. See the [3,1,0] run block below.\"}}, Frame -> All]]\n",
