   "kind": 1,
   "value": "### Task B result ([3,1,0], exact at P and P')\n\n**B1.** D1 has rank 7 and D2 (D1 + the 21 quadratic monomials of the six non-identity elements) rank 26 = 28 - 2: the two relations are the quadratic identities **S3c[1,1] = (1/4) S3c[1,2] (H1 - S3c[1,2])** and **S3c[2,1] = (1/4) S3c[2,2] (H2 - S3c[2,2])** (exact 225 x 225 operator identities at P, P' and four theta2 values; H2 = -H1 - W + 2|Lambda| Sum zeta). The localising space L = {X in D2 : <Omega (x) Omega|X in V (x) Omega1} has **dim L = 4, dim (L cap D1) = 3, quotient 1, l = 4** at both sites and both points (site 1: L cap D1 = {id, H1, S3c[1,2]}; site 2: {id, W+H1, S3c[2,2]}).\n\n**B2.** No support of size 1 works (none of H1^2, H1.S3c12, S3c12^2, S3c11, H1.S3c11, S3c12.S3c11, S3c11^2, W.H1, W.S3c12 localises with free D1 terms). Exactly **two minimal supports of size 2** and one of size 3 (their union) exist among the 1561 tested: {H1^2, H1.S3c12}, {H1^2, S3c12^2}, {H1^2, H1.S3c12, S3c12^2}. Explicit: **X4 = H1^2 - (1/2) H1.S3c12 - (2/theta12) W - S3c11** (mod id, H1, S3c12), equivalently (using the relation) H1^2 - (3/4) H1 S3c12 + (1/4) S3c12^2 - (2/theta12) W = (H1 - S3c12)(H1 - S3c12/4) - (2/theta12) W; the second representative is H1^2 - (1/2) S3c12^2 - (2/theta12) W - 3 S3c11. Site 2 mirror (H2t = H1 + W = -H2 + const): **X4' = H2t^2 + (1/2) H2t.S3c22 + (2/theta12) W - S3c21**. The coefficient 2/theta12 and all D1 coefficients are zeta- and omega-independent; the closed forms localise exactly at P (9 values of theta2) and P' (2 values).\n\n**B3.** v4 := the representative of v(X4) G-orthogonal (dual metric G^-1) to L1_3 = span{Omega1, v(H1), v(S3c12)}: **v4 is independent of theta12** (equal at 9 theta2), so its spectator f4 = v4[[1]] is a theta12-constant (Laurent fit degenerate: constant 3045512/34351321 at P for X4 normalised by its H1^2 coefficient 1; same value at site 2). Its one-site decomposition: v4 = Omega1.(c0 + c1 C_zeta + c2 S3^{1-site}[-2] - S3^{1-site}[-1] + C_zeta^2 + (1/2) C_zeta S3^{1-site}[-2]) — **three extra terms beyond {id, C_zeta, S3[-2]}**, minimal (three equivalent minimal sets because the ten candidate covectors have rank 9: {S3[-1], Cz^2, Cz.S3[-2]}, {S3[-1], Cz^2, S3[-2]^2}, {Cz^2, Cz.S3[-2], S3[-2]^2}); v4 lies in Omega1.(polynomials of degree <= 2 in {Cz, S3[-2], S3[-1]}), cyclic filtration dims 1, 4, 9, 15, 15. Weights: **the 3-dim L1 (and L2) already reaches every weight of V with full rank** (rank = multiplicity everywhere; the maximal weight multiplicity 2 is below 3), as does the 4-dim one: no weight fails, so the fourth localiser is not needed for per-weight rank; it is needed for the XXX-matching count l = lambda_1 + 1 = 4 and the localising-space dimension.\n\n**B4.** XXX rule for [3,1,0]: T_(1,1), T_(2,2), T_(3,2) at theta1 - 3h plus the identity = 4 = l1. Gaudin: id, H1 (= T_(1,1)), S3c[1,2] (= T_(2,2), the Laurent coefficient that plays T_(2,1) in the adjoint, found already in D1), and the third shape (3,2) is the QUADRATIC element X4 = (H1 - S3c[1,2])(H1 - S3c[1,2]/4) - (2/theta12) W, a product of two Laurent coefficients (degrees: T_(3,2) is cubic in T, the leading Gaudin term is quadratic in the Laurent coefficients); site 2: the mirror (H2t + S3c[2,2])(H2t + S3c[2,2]/4) + (2/theta12) W type element. This identification is a guess supported by the degrees, not an XXX computation.\n",
