   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## Task C: closed forms and universality\n### C1: c_H(Lambda, zeta, theta12) over eight (plus two) representations; fit of the 1/theta12 coefficient\n",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* Task C1. <Omega (x) Omega|H1 = [Omega1 (c_H - C_zeta)] (x) Omega1. With H1 = -[Sum_i zeta_i E1_ii + Sum_ik E1_ik E2_ki/theta12] + (|Lambda| Sum zeta + |Lambda|^2/theta12) id (exact operator identity from the cdet, verified in the Laurent cell for the run Lambda), the covector <Omega (x) Omega|E1_ik E2_ki = (Omega E_ik) (x) (Omega E_ki) is a ONE-SITE computation. Hence <Omega (x) Omega|H1 = [Omega1 (|Lambda| Sum zeta - C_zeta)] (x) Omega1 + (|Lambda|^2 Omega (x) Omega - T)/theta12, T := Sum_ik (Omega E_ik) (x) (Omega E_ki). Localisation holds iff T = t Omega (x) Omega (tested exactly for every representation, at 3 rational points (zeta, omega)); then c_H = |Lambda| Sum zeta + (|Lambda|^2 - t)/theta12. Representation-generic: JJ[i, j, rep] with its own rep argument, independent of the global switch Lambda. *)\nck = <||>;\nrowExpL[vv_, c_, M_, nl_] := vv + Sum[c^k/k! (vv . MatrixPower[M, k]), {k, 1, nl}];\nomOfRep[lam_, zz_, w12_] := Module[{d = dim[lam], nl = lam[[1]] - lam[[3]], Em, r = rGauss[zz, w12[[1]], w12[[2]]], v},\n  Em = Table[Normal[SparseArray[JJ[i, j, lam]]], {i, 3}, {j, 3}]; v = UnitVector[d, 1];\n  rowExpL[rowExpL[rowExpL[v, r[[1]], Em[[1, 2]], nl], r[[2]], Em[[1, 3]], nl], r[[3]], Em[[2, 3]], nl]];\ntOfRep[lam_, zz_, w12_] := Module[{d = dim[lam], Em = Table[Normal[SparseArray[JJ[i, j, lam]]], {i, 3}, {j, 3}], om = omOfRep[lam, zz, w12], T, OO},\n  OO = Flatten[KroneckerProduct[om, om]];\n  T = Sum[Flatten[KroneckerProduct[om . Em[[i, k]], om . Em[[k, i]]]], {i, 3}, {k, 3}];\n  {Union[T - (T[[1]]/OO[[1]]) OO] === {0}, T[[1]]/OO[[1]]}];\nc1Pts = {{zP, {5/2, 7/3}}, {zQ, {3, -1/3}}, {{-1, 7/3, 1/2}, {-3/2, 4/5}}};\nrepsC1 = {{1, 0, 0}, {1, 1, 0}, {2, 0, 0}, {2, 1, 0}, {2, 2, 0}, {3, 1, 0}, {3, 2, 0}, {4, 1, 0}, {3, 2, 1}, {2, 1, 1}};\nc1Data = Table[Module[{res = Table[tOfRep[lam, p[[1]], p[[2]]], {p, c1Pts}]},\n   <|\"lam\" -> lam, \"dim\" -> dim[lam], \"loc\" -> And @@ res[[All, 1]], \"t\" -> Union[res[[All, 2]]], \"sumsq\" -> Total[lam^2], \"L\" -> Total[lam]|>], {lam, repsC1}];\nc1Data = Map[Append[#, \"k\" -> (#[\"L\"]^2 - First[#[\"t\"]])] &, c1Data];\nck[\"T = t Omega (x) Omega exactly (localisation) for every representation at 3 points; t independent of (zeta, omega) (one value)\"] = And @@ (#[\"loc\"] && Length[#[\"t\"]] == 1 & /@ c1Data);\nck[\"t = Sum lambda_i^2 (Casimir of the top component 2 Lambda minus twice that of Lambda, halved) for every representation\"] = And @@ (First[#[\"t\"]] === #[\"sumsq\"] & /@ c1Data);\n(* fit of k = |Lambda|^2 - t as a polynomial in (l1, l2) for lambda3 = 0 reps: 6 fitting reps, 2 largest as checks *)\nfitReps = {{1, 0, 0}, {1, 1, 0}, {2, 0, 0}, {2, 1, 0}, {2, 2, 0}, {3, 1, 0}}; chkReps = {{3, 2, 0}, {4, 1, 0}};\nkOf[lam_] := First[Select[c1Data, #[\"lam\"] === lam &]][\"k\"];\npolyB[lam_] := {1, lam[[1]], lam[[2]], lam[[1]]^2, lam[[1]] lam[[2]], lam[[2]]^2};\nkfit = LinearSolve[Table[polyB[l], {l, fitReps}], Table[kOf[l], {l, fitReps}]];\nkfitPoly = kfit . {1, x1, x2, x1^2, x1 x2, x2^2};\nck[\"fit of the 1/theta12 coefficient k(l1, l2) on 6 reps (lambda3 = 0), as a polynomial in (l1, l2) = (x1, x2)\"] = kfitPoly;\nck[\"check of the fit on the two largest reps {3,2,0}, {4,1,0}: fit - exact\"] = Table[kfit . polyB[l] - kOf[l], {l, chkReps}];\nck[\"conjecture k = 2 l1 on all reps with lambda3 = 0: holds? (reps where it fails)\"] = Select[repsC1, #[[3]] == 0 && kOf[#] =!= 2 #[[1]] &];\nck[\"closed form k = |Lambda|^2 - Sum lambda_i^2 = 2 (l1 l2 + l1 l3 + l2 l3) on all 10 reps (including lambda3 != 0)\"] = And @@ (#[\"k\"] === 2 (#[\"lam\"][[1]] #[\"lam\"][[2]] + #[\"lam\"][[1]] #[\"lam\"][[3]] + #[\"lam\"][[2]] #[\"lam\"][[3]]) & /@ c1Data);\nchecks = Join[checks, ck];\nGrid[Join[{{\"Lambda\", \"dim\", \"|Lambda|\", \"localises\", \"t (T = t Omega (x) Omega)\", \"Sum lambda^2\", \"k = |Lambda|^2 - t\", \"c_H = |Lambda| Sum zeta + k/theta12\"}}, Table[{ToString[d[\"lam\"], InputForm], d[\"dim\"], d[\"L\"], d[\"loc\"], First[d[\"t\"]], d[\"sumsq\"], d[\"k\"], \"|Lambda| (z1+z2+z3) + \" <> ToString[d[\"k\"]] <> \"/theta12\"}, {d, c1Data}], List @@@ Normal[ck]], Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]\n",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "**[2,1,0] run** (the saved value of the switch):\n\n| Lambda | dim | \\|Lambda\\| | localises | t (T = t Omega (x) Omega) | Sum lambda^2 | k = \\|Lambda\\|^2 - t | c_H = \\|Lambda\\| Sum zeta + k/theta12 |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| {1, 0, 0} | 3 | 1 | True | 1 | 1 | 0 | \\|Lambda\\| (z1+z2+z3) + 0/theta12 |\n| {1, 1, 0} | 3 | 2 | True | 2 | 2 | 2 | \\|Lambda\\| (z1+z2+z3) + 2/theta12 |\n| {2, 0, 0} | 6 | 2 | True | 4 | 4 | 0 | \\|Lambda\\| (z1+z2+z3) + 0/theta12 |\n| {2, 1, 0} | 8 | 3 | True | 5 | 5 | 4 | \\|Lambda\\| (z1+z2+z3) + 4/theta12 |\n| {2, 2, 0} | 6 | 4 | True | 8 | 8 | 8 | \\|Lambda\\| (z1+z2+z3) + 8/theta12 |\n| {3, 1, 0} | 15 | 4 | True | 10 | 10 | 6 | \\|Lambda\\| (z1+z2+z3) + 6/theta12 |\n| {3, 2, 0} | 15 | 5 | True | 13 | 13 | 12 | \\|Lambda\\| (z1+z2+z3) + 12/theta12 |\n| {4, 1, 0} | 24 | 5 | True | 17 | 17 | 8 | \\|Lambda\\| (z1+z2+z3) + 8/theta12 |\n| {3, 2, 1} | 8 | 6 | True | 14 | 14 | 22 | \\|Lambda\\| (z1+z2+z3) + 22/theta12 |\n| {2, 1, 1} | 3 | 4 | True | 6 | 6 | 10 | \\|Lambda\\| (z1+z2+z3) + 10/theta12 |\n| T = t Omega (x) Omega exactly (localisation) for every representation at 3 points; t independent of (zeta, omega) (one value) | True |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| t = Sum lambda_i^2 (Casimir of the top component 2 Lambda minus twice that of Lambda, halved) for every representation | True |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| fit of the 1/theta12 coefficient k(l1, l2) on 6 reps (lambda3 = 0), as a polynomial in (l1, l2) = (x1, x2) | 2*x1*x2 |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| check of the fit on the two largest reps {3,2,0}, {4,1,0}: fit - exact | {0, 0} |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| conjecture k = 2 l1 on all reps with lambda3 = 0: holds? (reps where it fails) | {{1, 0, 0}, {2, 0, 0}, {2, 2, 0}, {3, 2, 0}} |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| closed form k = \\|Lambda\\|^2 - Sum lambda_i^2 = 2 (l1 l2 + l1 l3 + l2 l3) on all 10 reps (including lambda3 != 0) | True |  |  |  |  |  |  |",
