  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "### Task C result (closed forms, universality)\n\n**C1.** <Omega (x) Omega|H1 = [Omega1 (c_H - C_zeta)] (x) Omega1 with **c_H = |Lambda| (z1+z2+z3) + (|Lambda|^2 - Sum lambda_i^2)/theta12 = |Lambda| Sum zeta + 2 (l1 l2 + l1 l3 + l2 l3)/theta12**, checked exactly on 10 representations ({1,0,0}, {1,1,0}, {2,0,0}, {2,1,0}, {2,2,0}, {3,1,0}, {3,2,0}, {4,1,0}, {3,2,1}, {2,1,1}) at three (zeta, omega) points: T := Sum_ik (Omega E_ik) (x) (Omega E_ki) = t Omega (x) Omega with t = Sum lambda_i^2 (the Casimir of the top component 2 Lambda minus twice that of Lambda, halved; Omega (x) Omega lies in the Cartan product). The 1/theta12 coefficient k as a polynomial fitted on six lambda_3 = 0 reps is 2 l1 l2 (zero error on the two largest reps {3,2,0}, {4,1,0}); the conjectured 2 l1 holds only when l2 = 1 (fails for {1,0,0}, {2,0,0}, {2,2,0}, {3,2,0}).\n\n**C2.** Spectators: f(H1) = |Lambda| Sum zeta - zeta.Lambda + k/theta12, f(H2) = |Lambda| Sum zeta - zeta.Lambda - k/theta12 (independent of omega; k = 4 for [2,1,0], 6 for [3,1,0]); f(S3c[1,2]) = f(S3c[2,2]) = |Lambda| zeta_3 (3 z3, resp. 4 z3), independent of omega1, omega2 and theta (derived from the one-site identity <Omega (x) Omega|S3c[1,2] = [Omega1 S3^{1-site}[-2]] (x) Omega1, symbolic in zeta, omega); verified exactly against the full two-site spectators at 9 (zeta, theta) combinations for both reps ([2,1,0]: 6 + 4/theta12 and 2 at P; [3,1,0]: 95/12 + 6/theta12 and 8/3).\n\n**C3.** Vacuum eigenvalue functions (zeta-independent; derived from e1 (x) e1 being the common eigencovector of the diag(omega)-twisted model, symbolic in omega1..3, theta12): S2(infinity) = e2(omega), S3(infinity) = e3(omega); S2 double pole |Lambda| (3, 4); **H_s^vac = sum_i (|Lambda| - lambda_i) omega_i +/- k/theta12** ([2,1,0]: omega1 + 2 omega2 + 3 omega3 +/- 4/theta12; [3,1,0]: omega1 + 3 omega2 + 4 omega3 +/- 6/theta12); S3 triple pole 0, **a_s^vac = |Lambda| omega3**, **b_s^vac = omega3 (H_s^vac - |Lambda| omega3)** (= omega3 (omega1 + 2 omega2 +/- 4/theta12) for [2,1,0]). Verified exactly against the two-site eigencovector at P, P', and omega = wP, wpP, wQ (and reproduces H1 = 12539/930, H2 = 4139/930, a_s = 9/5, b1 = 2173/310, b2 = 493/310 of round 1).\n\n**C4.** At g = 0 the matrix of S3c[1,2] on the exact HW kets of a multiplicity-2 sector is **purely (1/theta12) times a theta-independent matrix, no scalar part (s = 0)**: [3,2,1] (adjoint): (3/(2 theta12)) [[3,-1],[-1,7]]; [3,1,0] (5,2,1): (1/(3 theta12)) [[19,-40],[-2,44]]; (4,3,1): (4/(3 theta12)) [[4,-1],[-2,14]] (checked at theta12 = 31/35, 29/45, 19/28; zeta plays no role at g = 0, so P and P' coincide). The eigenvectors are therefore universal, and so is the mixing: the ratio r = c2/c1 of the two HW-ket coordinates of the copies solves r^2 + 4r - 1 = 0 ([3,2,1]: r = -2 +/- sqrt 5), 40 r^2 + 25 r - 2 = 0 ((5,2,1): r = (-25 +/- 3 sqrt 105)/80 = 0.0718, -0.6968), r^2 + 10 r - 2 = 0 ((4,3,1): r = -5 +/- 3 sqrt 3 = 0.1962, -10.196); the true copies (eigenvectors of S2(u) + Pi S3(u') on the HW space) have the same ratios at every theta (difference 0 to 14 digits). Hence R^2 - 5R - 5 = 0 (adjoint) and R = 4.3117..., -0.8117... ((5,2,1)) are universal.\n",
