   "value": "### sl(3) Gaudin L = 2 chain, part 2 (2026-10-16)\n\n**A. The (inf,inf) family (both reps): CG-complete, all chain-side data verified.** Phi^inf = OmegaDinf[zeta,om1] (x) OmegaDinf[zeta,om1'] with the closed forms r_k^inf (om2 -> infinity limits of the round-1 r_k; relative convergence 6.4e-7 at om2 = 1e6) is the unique common eigencovector of the top-degree-in-om2 Laurent operators (finite limit exists). Companion frame: Omega_c[om] has Gauss parameters (1/om1, -1/(om1 om2), (om1+om2)/(om1 om2)) -> (1/om1, 0, 1/om1) at om2 = infinity (alpha = gamma = 1/om1, om3-free); frame tie OmegaD.PphysG parallel to Omega_c exactly with kappa^G = XXX kappaTie formula for P3 = (PauxG^-1)^T. Exact undo; undone parameters a' = (z1-z2)(om1-om1')/((z2-om1)(z2-om1')), c' = (z1-z3)(z2-z3)(om1-om1')/((z1-z2)(z3-om1)(z3-om1')), g' = (z3-z1)(z3-z2)(om1-om1')/((z3-om1)(z2-om1')(z3-om1')), eps-free, Jacobian rank 2; per-weight ranks = multiplicities on every weight (4-point grid) for both reps; K/S = O(eps) for every HW branch (ratio 2.000), S = O(1); CG slices (1-dim and 2-dim) and the mixing roots of R^2 - 5R - 5 = 0 ([3,1,0] (5,2,1): 4.3117, -0.8117) reproduced to 1e-18 .. 1e-21 after Richardson. Controls: om1' = om1 reads only the top branch; om1' = 7/4 fixed with om2 = infinity FAILS (singlet-type K/S = O(1), 2-dim slices wrong), unlike round 1 at finite om2. Reference tables A5 (Qnum, equal-twist and Phi^inf overlaps, eigenvalue pairs, 30 digits) at P, P' (all states) and the regime point (HW branches), both reps.\n\n**B. The [3,1,0] fourth localiser.** dim L = 4 (D2 rank 26 = 28 - 2 quadratic relations S3c[s,1] = (1/4) S3c[s,2] (H_s - S3c[s,2])), L cap D1 = 3, quotient 1. No single quadratic monomial suffices; minimal supports {H1^2, H1.S3c12} and {H1^2, S3c12^2}: X4 = H1^2 - (1/2) H1 S3c12 - (2/theta12) W - S3c11 = (H1 - S3c12)(H1 - S3c12/4) - (2/theta12) W (mod id, H1, S3c12); site 2 mirror with H2t = H1 + W. v4 is theta12-independent (spectator constant), v4 = Omega1.(Cz^2 + (1/2) Cz S3[-2] - S3[-1] + L1_3 terms); the 3-dim L1 already reaches every weight (multiplicity <= 2 < 3). XXX guess: the third shape T_(3,2) <-> X4.\n\n**C. Closed forms.** c_H = |Lambda| Sum zeta + (|Lambda|^2 - Sum lambda^2)/theta12 (2 l1 l2 for lambda3 = 0; the conjecture 2 l1 is refuted); f(H1) = |Lambda| Sum zeta - zeta.Lambda + k/theta12, f(S3c[1,2]) = |Lambda| zeta3; vacuum eigenvalues H_s = Sum (|Lambda| - lambda_i) omega_i +/- k/theta12, a_s = |Lambda| omega3, b_s = omega3 (H_s - |Lambda| omega3); S3c[1,2]|_HW (g = 0) = (1/theta12) x (theta-independent matrix), so eigenvectors and mixing roots are universal ((5,2,1): 40 r^2 + 25 r - 2 = 0, (4,3,1): r^2 + 10 r - 2 = 0 for the HW-ket coordinate ratio; adjoint r^2 + 4r - 1 = 0).\n\n**Surprises.** (i) om1' fixed control fails for the (inf,inf) family (it passed at finite om2 in round 1). (ii) Laurent operators are degree 1 in om2 (also S3). (iii) the [3,1,0] fourth localiser is a combination of two quadratic monomials with a W term (2/theta12) and S3c[s,1] is NOT independent: two exact quadratic identities in D2. (iv) the 3-dim L1 does not miss any weight, contrary to the guess that it fails on one. (v) the 1/theta12 coefficient of c_H is 2 e2(Lambda), not 2 l1. (vi) pitfall: Laurent fits at theta1 = 3/7 = u0 hit a pole (fixed with alternative sample points `uSamAlt`; memoised `laurent` caches bad values).\n\n**Not done / caveats.** The literal rescaled-twist test S2^{(g'/om2)}, S3^{(g'/om2^2)} was replaced by the equivalent top-degree-in-om2 operator test (the S3 scaling is om2^1, not om2^2). The XXX identification in B4 is a guess from degrees. No native outputs are stored (rerun in VS Code); results are the markdown cells below each code cell.\n",
